*Probability Current:* The probability current density $j$ represents the flow of probability. In 1D, it is related to the wavefunction by $j = planck/m Im(psi^* dif / (dif x) psi)$. The net momentum expectation value relates to the spatial integral of the current by $chevron.l p chevron.r = m integral_(-infinity)^infinity j(x) dif x$.
